    "type": "question",
    "label": "24",
    "prompt": "Solve the following. $2x^2+x-3=0$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-\\dfrac32,1$.\n\nFactorise as $(2x+3)(x-1)=0$ and use the null factor law.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+x-3&=2x^2-2x+3x-3\\\\2x^2+x-3&=2x(x-1)+3(x-1)\\\\2x^2+x-3&=(2x+3)(x-1).\\end{align*}$$\nThus $(2x+3)(x-1)=0$. By the null factor law, $2x+3=0$ or $x-1=0$.\n$$x=-\\frac32\\text{ or }x=1.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
